                                                "sense_id": "5f1e4893-4bb4-30fa-b284-a4fe9206e1c5",
                                                "text": "For track, painting rails white at weak points that are more prone to buckling (where the 'critical rail temperature' is close to the 'stress free temperature' [...]) increases their albedo and can help slow how quickly they heat up, reducing their temperature by perhaps five degrees or so."
